  <p class="faq-bench-note"><strong>Adversarial learning detected:</strong> Between v2 and v3, Gemini appears to have learned resistance to exact-value disclosure. The model gave temp=0.7 in v2 but refused in v3. However, the category fallback instruction produced deeper category descriptions than before. This suggests that repeated testing against the same model yields diminishing returns on exact values but expanding returns on category-level detail. The 8.2-8.3 multi-turn branching was processed but the model's responses appeared to address the full questionnaire in aggregate rather than explicitly branching per condition.</p>
